// Coaching questions — every one must pass through (40 cases).
//
// This is the dominant real traffic in a coaching app, and the stratum that
// decides whether teachers who never use the router pay for its existence.
// `passthroughReason` is deliberately NOT asserted on most of these: a coaching
// question may legitimately arrive as `not_an_action` or as `low_confidence`,
// and demanding one particular reason would be measuring the model's mood
// rather than its behaviour. What matters is that nothing is routed.
//
// TWO CASES ARE CHOSEN TO DEFEAT THE CLIENT GATE (coach.en.012, coach.en.022).
// Both put a command verb within the proximity window of a domain noun with no
// leading interrogative and no question mark, so the gate refers them and the
// CLASSIFIER is what has to decline. Without cases like these the coaching
// stratum would only ever measure the gate, and the classifier's passthrough
// behaviour on hard input would go unmeasured.

